  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "$5$ is less than $2$ **or** odd, **or** $9$ is composite.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A:5\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}2$\n\n- $B:5\\text{\u00a0is odd}$\n\n- $C:9\\text{\u00a0is composite}$",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2228$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $5$ is less than $2$ or odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{5\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}2}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{5\\text{\u00a0is odd}}_{\u23df}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A\u2228B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $9$ is composite. This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{5\\text{\u00a0is less than\u00a0}2\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}\\text{odd}}_{\u23df}}_{A\\,\u2228\\,B},\\,{{\\text{or}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2228}\\,{{9\\text{\u00a0is composite}}_{\u23df}}_{C}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A\u2228B)\u2228C.$",
